// of `rules/protocol-events.md` (2026-11-15, baseline `d8a9061a`), the 309
// rows of `rules/protocol-runtime.md` (2026-11-15, baseline `b3bd09e4`) and the
// 248 rows of `rules/protocol-remote.md` (2026-11-15, baseline `5b2b8674`).
//
// The re-check in `formal-trace-recheck.mjs` maps a rule onto a current source;
// it does not rewrite the rule. This table is the rewrite, in two forms:
//
//   - A trace row (`SEMANTIC`, `translate: true`) is rewritten whole: the
//     section of the current source (`source`, a file plus a section), the
//     `SESS-*` anchors of `docs/protocol-session.md` §11 that carry the rule
//     (`anchorKind: 'session'`), the rule text in force in English (`en`; the
//     Chinese row in the file is the same rule) and its English gap (`gapEn`).
//   - A protocol-list row (`translate: false`) is the issue row the partition
//     exported; its rule wording is the issue snapshot's and is not rewritten.
//     What is re-extracted is the current source, the current anchor, the
//     evidence the current tree holds (`evidence`) and the status (`status`),
//     with the reason in `why`/`whyEn`. The registry partitions (`SEMANTIC_*`)
//     anchor on guarantee-register rows (`anchorKind: 'register'`); the session
//     partition (`SEMANTIC_SESSION`) anchors on a `SESS-*` rule where the
//     session specification carries the rule and on a register row where the
//     register does (`anchorKind: 'mixed'`); the events partition
//     (`SEMANTIC_EVENTS`) anchors on the event protocol's own section or §15
//     decision, on a `SESS-*` rule where the session specification carries it,
//     or on a register row (`anchorKind: 'events'`).
//
// `anchors: []` requires `whyNoAnchor`/`whyNoAnchorEn`: the partition's
// document does not cover the rule, and the row says where it lives instead.
// `extra` names a second current source the row also cites. `source: '0.22
// 无此条'` (with `sourceEn`) says no current document states the rule at all; it
// cannot be anchored.
//
// This file is the single source of the generated English re-check page
// (`docs/formal-trace/recheck-0.22.en.md`) and of the semantic sections of the
// Chinese re-check page. `formal-trace.mjs --check` verifies: every row of each
// partition's file has one entry and the reverse, every entry's status equals
// the re-checked status of its row, every anchor exists (a `SESS-*` id in the
// session specification, an `EVP` / `EVD` section or decision in the event
// protocol, or a register row in the section the entry names),
// every `source` (and `extra`) section heading exists in its document, every
// backticked evidence path resolves and every named test is defined in it, and
// both generated pages match. The six protocol partitions below are
// re-extracted here: `registry-1`, `registry-2`, `session`, `events`, `runtime`
// and `remote` all keep the issue's rule wording and re-extract the source, the
// anchor, the evidence and the status.
